---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About" description="A longer introduction — professionally and otherwise.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>The longer version</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-body">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I’ve spent most of my career in procurement and third-party risk
          management — the unglamorous machinery of how large organizations
          decide who to work with and how to handle the consequences. I like
          this work, which surprises people. The interesting parts of business
          happen at the boundaries between organizations, and I get to live
          there.
        </p>

        <p>
          Outside of that, I run a small HOA, manage a rental property a few
          states away, build furniture in a workshop slowly accumulating
          better tools, ride a motorcycle on long, deliberately scenic routes,
          cook a lot, and read more philosophy than is probably useful. None
          of these are hobbies in the dabbling sense. They’re different rooms
          in the same house — and they’re what this site is mostly about.
        </p>

        <h2>Professionally</h2>

        <p>
          I lead transformation work on a Third Party Risk Management (TPRM)
          team at a large organization. The work spans operating-model
          design, platform evaluation, executive communication, and the
          long, patient business of moving institutional consensus.
          Confidentiality keeps most of the specifics off this site, but a
          short version of what I’m good at:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>
            Translating between people who think in spreadsheets and people
            who think in metaphors
          </li>
          <li>
            Designing processes that survive contact with a real
            organization
          </li>
          <li>
            Knowing when something needs more rigor and when it needs less
          </li>
          <li>
            Telling executives uncomfortable things in a way they can hear
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          A longer professional record, with current role and selected
          initiatives, lives on my <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/yourhandle">LinkedIn</a>.
          If you want to talk about work specifically — current role, past
          roles, or what I might do next — email is best.
        </p>

        <h2>What I’m working out</h2>

        <p>
          How to operate at the boundary where human judgment and machine
          capability meet — not as theatre, but as actual practice. Most of
          what gets called “AI strategy” inside large companies is still
          downstream of pre-AI assumptions, and the work of redesigning from
          first principles is harder and slower than anyone wants to admit.
          I write about this occasionally in the
          <a href="/writing">writing section</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How to reach me</h2>

        <p>
          Email is best: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
          I read everything, reply to most things, and reply to the
          interesting things faster than I should.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 720px; }
  .page-hero { padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-l); }
  .page-hero .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .page-hero h1 { font-size: var(--step-5); font-weight: 300; }
  .about-body { padding-block: var(--space-l) var(--space-2xl); }
</style>
